Source: asys
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Roman <roman@nekko.ai>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-python, python3, golang-1.25-go | golang-go (>= 2:1.25~)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/glguida/asys
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: asys
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.10), dcomp (>= 0.3.1), asys-images (>= ${source:Upstream-Version}), asys-images (<< ${source:Upstream-Version}+), docker.io | docker-ce
Recommends: git
Description: agent execution environment with logged runs and shared inference
 asys runs LLM agents, goals, BPMN workflows, programs and human requests
 in Docker environments through dcomp, recording every job. This package
 installs the host commands (asys, asys-run, asys-workers, asys-environment,
 asys-inference, asys-human-prompt), the bundled operating and authoring
 skills, dashboard designs, system agents and examples.

Package: asys-server
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, asys (>= ${source:Version}), adduser, python3
Recommends: nginx
Description: shared team deployment of asys under /srv/asys
 Creates the asys group and service user, initializes group-shared asys and
 dcomp state under /srv/asys, runs the dashboard as a system service, and
 provides asys-adduser, asys-skills and asys-server-update helpers. On
 upgrade it refreshes running shared services with "asys update".
